cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use IxD Lab in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "IxD Lab: An AI-Powered Learning and Experimentation Environment for Interaction Design"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-01
authors:
  - family-names: "Sánchez-Núñez"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    email: psancheznunez@outlook.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7845-9506"
url: "https://pablosancheznunez.com/ixd-lab/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pablosancheznunez/ixd-lab"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  IxD Lab is an open educational resource for learning interaction design by
  making, testing, and reflecting. Six browser-based labs cover wireframing,
  information architecture, usability, accessibility, interaction patterns,
  and user behaviour. The software is released under the MIT License and the
  educational content under CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - interaction design
  - user experience
  - human-computer interaction
  - open educational resources
  - OER
  - Shiny
  - R
